## 1. Reconnaissance & Enumeration
We begin by running an `nmap` scan against the target IP address (`10.129.229.66`) to discover open ports and services.

```bash
nmap 10.129.229.66
The scan reveals two open ports:   Port 22/tcp: SSH   Port 80/tcp: HTTP (2million.htb)
Finding the Invite PortalNavigating to http://2million.htb/invite in our browser presents an invite code prompt. 
Inspecting the page source reveals a JavaScript reference to /js/inviteapi.min.js which handles verification and form submission. 
3. Enumerating API Endpoints & Decoding the Invite CodeWe query the /api/v1/invite/how/to/generate endpoint using curl to find out how to get an invite code:   
curl -sX POST [http://2million.htb/api/v1/invite/how/to/generate](http://2million.htb/api/v1/invite/how/to/generate) | jq
The server returns a ROT13-encrypted message indicating we need to make a POST request to /api/v1/invite/generate
Next, we request the invite code from the generated endpoint and decode the resulting base64 string:
curl -sX POST [http://2million.htb/api/v1/invite/generate](http://2million.htb/api/v1/invite/generate) | jq
echo "VjlYODEtNkJIUzktQjlUODMtMlMzTFo=" | base64 -d
Decoded Invite Code: V9X81-6BHS9-B9T83-2S3LZ

